## Smell-Free Pattern

`ValidateOrder_NullOrder_ThrowsArgumentNullException` (line 155) is clean: it uses `Assert.ThrowsException<T>` for exception testing, asserts on a specific property (`ParamName`), has no magic numbers, and exercises exactly one production method. This is the model to follow.

